===============================================================================
                                   PREAMBLE
===============================================================================

Betazen Server Panel is published as SOURCE-AVAILABLE software. The source
code is openly published so that operators can audit it, contribute fixes,
self-host it for their own infrastructure, and learn from it. It is NOT
"open source" within the strict meaning of the Open Source Initiative
because this license imposes restrictions on commercial redistribution and
competing hosted services.

If those restrictions are unacceptable to you, do not copy, modify, or
distribute this software. Instead, contact licensing@betazeninfotech.com
to negotiate a commercial license.

This license is intended to:

  (a) give every user broad, perpetual rights to self-host, modify, and
      audit the software for internal use,
  (b) prevent third parties from offering Betazen Server Panel, or a
      derivative of it, as a competing commercial hosting-control-panel
      service without a separate written agreement with BetaZen InfoTech,
  (c) require all public-facing derivatives to share their modifications
      back under this same license (strong copyleft), and
  (d) protect the "BetaZen" and "Betazen Server Panel" trademarks from
      confusingly similar forks.

